// Title: Potential Persistence Via AutodialDLL
// Sigma ID: e6fe26ee-d063-4f5b-b007-39e90aaf50e3
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-10 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects change the the "AutodialDLL" key which could be used as a persistence method to load
//   custom DLL via the "ws2_32" library
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2015/01/13/beyond-good-ol-run-key-part-24/
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/autodialdll.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_autodial_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Services\\WinSock2\\Parameters\\AutodialDLL"
